<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Personal | Egor Shulgin</title><link>https://shulgin-egor.github.io/personal/</link><atom:link href="https://shulgin-egor.github.io/personal/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><description>Personal</description><generator>Source Themes Academic (https://sourcethemes.com/academic/)</generator><language>en-us</language><image><url>img/map[gravatar:%!s(bool=false) shape:circle]</url><title>Personal</title><link>https://shulgin-egor.github.io/personal/</link></image><item><title>Personal</title><link>https://shulgin-egor.github.io/personal/</link><pubDate>Mon, 04 Jan 2021 00:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://shulgin-egor.github.io/personal/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="short-bio">Short Bio&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>I was born in the Almaty city (Kazakhstan) surrounded by wondeful mountains. When I was two years old, my family moved to Samara city in Russia, where I lived until the start of my undegraduate studies.
My studies started at Gymnasium # 11 with focus on foreign (English) language. At 8th grade I transfered to technical departement of Medical-Technical Lyceem and spent most of the time on maths, physics and informatics.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="hobbies">Hobbies&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>I got started in tourism (mostly backpacking/hiking and water tourism) thanks to my homeroom teacher, head of the Lyceum tourist club. We were lucky to visit Caucasus, Khibiny, Taganai, Altai, Tien Shan (around Lake Issyk-Kul in Kyrgyzstan).&lt;/p>
